menu "CSI receiver configuration"

    config CSI_RX_CHANNEL
        int "Channel to listen on"
        range 1 177
        default 36
        help
            Must match CSI_TX_CHANNEL on the transmitter board exactly.

    config CSI_RX_FILTER_MAC
        string "Only report CSI from this transmitter MAC"
        default "00:00:00:00:00:00"
        help
            Format aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff. The transmitter prints its own address at
            boot; paste it here.

            Leave it all zeros to report CSI from every transmitter on the
            channel, which is what you want when you are still checking that
            anything arrives at all.

    config CSI_RX_PRINT_CSV
        bool "Print the full CSV line per record"
        default y
        help
            Turn this off to keep only the one-line AMP summary, which is far
            easier to read while you are physically moving around the room.

    config CSI_RX_FORCE_LLTF
        bool "Report L-LTF instead of HT/VHT/HE-LTF"
        default n
        help
            Maps to acquire_csi_force_lltf. Say n for the full HE-LTF
            resolution the C5 is capable of - 8-bit int8 pairs, two bytes per
            tone, 245 tones for an HE20 frame.

            Say y for L-LTF: always a 106-byte record whatever the transmitter
            used. Note that L-LTF on the C5 defaults to 12-bit packing, which is
            four bytes per tone and 26 tones - undocumented, and the usual cause
            of silently wrong CSI on this chip. The shared component handles it
            and reports which format each record used in the "packing" column.

            In this example the transmitter's PHY is pinned anyway, so record
            shape is already stable and there is little reason to force L-LTF.

    config CSI_RX_VAL_SCALE
        int "CSI value scaling (val_scale_cfg)"
        range 0 8
        default 0
        help
            Scales the reported I/Q values. ESP-IDF documents only the range,
            0-8 on the C5, so this is a knob to sweep rather than one to reason
            about. Start at 0 and change it only if the AMP figures clip or
            vanish into the noise.

endmenu
